6:A resident grain's program (`pkg/resident`), confined by grain-launch like any grain. It can see its
7:package (read), its volume (read and write), its own broker socket and its own member socket, and
8:nothing else. Its argv must be its plan (`Args.place`), or it ends `argvNotPlan` before reading
9:anything. It reads `pkg/resident.conf`, ONE Lang data value at `Bell.confTy`. Then, every
10:`tickMs`, for at most `lifetimeTicks` ticks:
11:1. Until it has the bell's shape, it describes the bell (`read OBJ ?` → `Shape.read`); a package
12:   that is not the Bell ends it `bellShape notBell` (HOSTING-45).
13:2. It reads every pending ring in ONE read (`read OBJ pending K`, K = `pending`'s declared limit →
14:   `Ring.readAll`), lowest first.
15:3. It acts on `decideTick`:
16:   - idle: forget a kept answer whose ring is no longer pending;
17:   - ask (the lowest pending ring, when no kept ring is pending): first keep the intent
18:     (`(unanswered restart)`) for the ring, keyed by its `(notBefore, ringer)` and its text, then
80:verdict (any exit counts toward `crashLoop`); each code names one case on stderr. -/
